<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Nexus.Intelligence.LiveSmokeTests</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Nexus.Intelligence.LiveSmokeTests</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- W7G.2 GATE 9: the provider-specific AI Head smoke suite.

       The three assertions here are the M-01-6.1 smoke checks (migration runbook items 12-14)
       that samples\Nexus.Platform.SmokeHost used to carry at the Platform layer. The ownership
       decision re-homed them: provider-specific OpenAI / Anthropic / model smoke and E2E testing
       belongs to the AI Head, and Platform smoke is provider-neutral.

       THIS PROJECT IS DELIBERATELY NOT IN Nexus.Intelligence.slnx, AND THE REASON IS DIFFERENT
       FROM ITS PREDECESSOR'S.

       The retired Platform suite was outside its solution because it could only run by hand, and
       that is precisely how it rotted: it held a ProjectReference to a project that had been
       deleted, and because nothing built it, nothing was red. Its being outside the solution was
       not the root cause, but it removed the only signal that would have caught the cause.

       The reason here is that these tests SPEND THE OWNER'S MONEY. Every run calls OpenAI. Putting
       them in the solution would make every `dotnet test` in every future lane a paid vendor call,
       and that is a decision with a cost that nobody asked this lane to make.

       So the anti-rot signal is supplied separately, where it cannot be missed:
       Nexus.Intelligence.Architecture.Tests.LiveSmokeProjectIntegrityTests asserts, IN the
       solution and on every run, that this project's references all resolve and that this project
       is still deliberately outside the solution. The failure that destroyed the predecessor is
       therefore caught by a test that runs always, without spending anything. -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Nexus.Intelligence.LiveSmokeHost\Nexus.Intelligence.LiveSmokeHost.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="3.1.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
